# App Shell Contract

- `App.tsx` may bootstrap the OS. It may not define the OS.
- Keep `App.tsx` limited to providers, router mount, and shell mount.
- Do not place business logic, prompt logic, or giant route trees in `App.tsx`.
- The shell must preserve a persistent `ContextBar`, breadcrumbs, conversational navigation surface, and primary chat/PTT container.
- Respect shell modes from `docs-governance/APP_SHELL_CONTRACT.md`: `menu`, `view`, `confirmation`, `refusal`, `ptt_first`.
